<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>CPAN::InGit repository</title>
  <style>
    body { font: 1rem/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 50rem; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; color: #172331; }
    a { color: #165ca2; } li { margin: .5rem 0; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main>
    <h1>CPAN::InGit repository</h1>
    <p>This is the root of a CPAN::InGit repository. Each archive branch provides its own CPAN mirror, with package versions stored in Git.</p>
    <p>To make changes, work in a local clone of this repository. Use <code>cpangit-create</code> to create an archive branch if needed, then check out the branch you want to update and run <code>cpangit-add</code> with module names or a cpanfile to import packages and their dependencies. Review the staged changes with <code>git diff --cached</code>, commit them with <code>git commit</code>, and push the branch to the repository served here.</p>
    <p>See the <a href="https://metacpan.org/pod/CPAN::InGit">CPAN::InGit documentation</a> for setup and usage details.</p>
% if ($index_branches) {
    <section id="branch-index" aria-labelledby="branches-heading">
      <h2 id="branches-heading">Available branches</h2>
% if (@$branches) {
      <ul>
% for my $branch (@$branches) {
        <li><a href="<%= $branch->{url} %>"><%= $branch->{name} %></a></li>
% }
      </ul>
% } else {
      <p>No CPAN archive branches are available.</p>
% }
    </section>
% }
  </main>
</body>
</html>
